> [MAN]ILA, Philippines — The state-run Land Bank of the Philippines (Landbank) has extended by one more month or until[ Jan].[ 31] next year its revised offer to buy out existing[ Philippine] Dealing System Holdings Corp. (PDS) shareholders and gain control of the bond exchange.
In a text message[ Friday], Landbank[ president Alex] V. Buenaventura said the offer period was moved from the earlier deadline of end-[December] 2018 as there was “no response so far[�]� from PDS shareholders.
